# netconsole — kernel messages that survive the hang that produced them.
#
# This lab has no serial console attached (B-1's FTDI cable is not in the rig),
# and the two other ways of reading dmesg both need the machine to still be
# working: SSH needs userspace, and pstore/ramoops needs the RAM contents to
# survive the reset, which on a hard RGU watchdog reset here they do not — a
# blank /sys/fs/pstore after a real hang, 2026-08-21.
#
# So a hang currently leaves NO evidence at all. `xset dpms force off` wedged
# the kernel hard enough that the watchdog took 5 minutes to reclaim it and
# there was nothing afterwards to say where it went. netconsole streams kernel
# messages over the USB gadget as they are printed, so the last line before a
# wedge is already on the host.
#
# Built in rather than modular so it can be armed from the kernel command line
# before any userspace exists; DYNAMIC additionally allows reconfiguring the
# target over configfs once the gadget interface is up, which is how the lab
# uses it (see scripts/gemini-netconsole.sh).
CONFIG_NETCONSOLE=y
CONFIG_NETCONSOLE_DYNAMIC=y
CONFIG_CONFIGFS_FS=y
